Monte Carlo sampling of the spins (fix mc/spin)
===============================================

  in.spin.mc      fcc cobalt on a frozen lattice: Metropolis sampling of the
                  spin directions at 300 K.  The cone of trial directions is
                  adapted during a first run and then kept fixed for the
                  production run.

  in.spin.mc_md   fcc cobalt with moving atoms: fix mc/spin samples the spin
                  directions and magnitudes (modulus walk) with the Landau
                  energy of fix landau/spin, while fix nve and fix langevin
                  integrate and thermostat the atoms.

Both inputs require the SPIN and MANYBODY packages and use the Co potential
of the cobalt_fcc example.  Run them from this directory:

  lmp -in in.spin.mc
  lmp -in in.spin.mc_md

Each process draws its own random numbers, so the logs for 1 and 4
processes differ.  In parallel, every subdomain must be at least twice as
wide as the spin cutoff, hence the 6x6x6 cell.
